; =============================================================================
; UI Widget Descriptor System (internal codename: "NAKA")
; =============================================================================
;
; This subsystem defines the hierarchical UI screen layouts used throughout
; the KN5000 firmware. Each screen is described as a tree of typed widget
; descriptors (containers, lists, bitmaps, panels, dialogs, etc.) that the
; UI framework traverses to render and dispatch events.
;
; "NAKA" is the Matsushita/Technics developer codename for this subsystem.
; All original symbol names (InitializeNaka, NAKA_TYPE_*, etc.) are preserved.
;
; Files in this directory:
;   widget_descriptors.s  - Widget type definitions and descriptor tables
;   widget_dispatch.s     - Widget event dispatch and screen routing
;   style_bitmaps.s       - Style selection bitmap resources
;   e*_e*.s               - Screen descriptor data blocks (named by ROM address range)
;   block_*.s             - Additional descriptor blocks
; =============================================================================

